-- title:
--   Igusa-branch place at a node of the semistable model
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$.
--
--   **Modular data.** $W$ is a finite set of places of the field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\operatorname{ResidueField} A, M')$ — the subfield of $\operatorname{ResidueField}(A)$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $M'$ — over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places for $q$: the rational places $w$ which are affine geometric places (`IsAffineGeomPlace`) and for which $w$ evaluated at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. A member $s\in W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar } M' \le \mathtt{fieldBar } q\, M'$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` (the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`).
--
--   **The reduction datum $R_0$.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar } M'$ to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\operatorname{ResidueField} A, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting the constants exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction of constants, such that every nonzero element becomes an element with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that this reduction is coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar } M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and the Laurent series underlying its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField} A$.
--
--   **The characterisation `hGU` of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$.** For every valuation subring $V$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar } M'$ such that (i) a constant $a\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has its image in $V$ precisely when $a\in A$, (ii) $V$ contains the element $j$ obtained as the coefficientwise image of the Laurent expansion `jq`, and (iii) for every polynomial $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(j)$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$ then every coefficient of $p$ has its image in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$, the subring $V$ has the same elements as $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$.
--
--   **The small-constants block.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ has image in $A$; writing $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$), the hypotheses require that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is Henselian local, and that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; finally `hκ` requires that every $a\in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$.
--
--   The conclusion is formulated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathtt{fieldBar } q\, M'$ obtained by composing $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the structure map, and is a universally quantified statement over the following further data.
--
--   **The level field $F_0$.** An intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathtt{fieldBar } q\, M'$ over $k_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is everything, and such that the following linear-disjointness condition holds: for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to \mathtt{fieldBar } q\, M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ then every $a_i=0$.
--
--   **The supersingular valuation ring $W_0$.** A valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ subject to a three-clause hypothesis: an element $x\in k_0$ lies in $A$ precisely when its image in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   **The node ring $O$.** A subring $O$ of $F_0$, local and Noetherian, with $O\subseteq W_0$; an element $x\in k_0$ lies in $A$ precisely when its image lies in $O$; every $f\in O$ differs by a nonunit of $O$ from (the image of) some $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$ and image in $O$; and $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$, in the form that every $f\in F_0$ satisfies $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in O$ with $h\ne 0$.
--
--   **The crossing presentation.** A natural number $E_0\ge 1$, the membership of the image of $\pi_0$ in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}$ of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is onto $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that quotient, subject to: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends the image of a constant $x\in k_0$ (lying in $A$ and with image in $O$) to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\widehat{A_0}$; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; and, on the $W_0$-side, $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   **The Igusa branch $W_x$.** A valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with $O\subseteq W_x$; an element $x\in k_0$ lies in $A$ precisely when its image lies in $W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_x$ and generates its maximal ideal; there is $t\in W_x$ with the Gauss-type property that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ while $c_y$, whenever it lies in $W_x$, does not. The last clause of this block relates $W_x$, $O$ and $R_0$: for every Laurent series $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field whose coefficientwise image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and which satisfies the order condition that at every place $P$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar } M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j$ has non-negative order the element $g$ also has non-negative order, the image of $g$ under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$; that element of $F_0$ lies in $W_x$; it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ is $0$; and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then that element of $F_0$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ and with image in $O$ whose reduction in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the two elements of $O$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   **The prolongation $R_x$.** A field $FI$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and a `RegularProlongation` $R_x$ of $A$ from $\mathtt{fieldBar } q\, M'$ to $FI$ (a valuation subring $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting the constants exactly in $A$, with a surjective residue map to $FI$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction of constants, and such that every nonzero element has nonzero residue after scaling by a constant), whose trace on $F_0$ is $W_x$: for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f\in W_x$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of these hypotheses there exists a place $b_x$ of $FI$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ such that:
--
--   1. $b_x$ is rational, i.e. the structure map from $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ to the residue field of $b_x$ is surjective;
--
--   2. for every $f\in F_0$ lying in $O$ and in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$, the $R_x$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$;
--
--   3. for every such $f$ which moreover is not a unit of $O$, the $R_x$-residue of $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of the valuation subring of $b_x$;
--
--   4. $b_x$ is the unique place with these two properties: any place $y$ of $FI$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ such that the $R_x$-residue of every $f\in O\cap R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the valuation subring of $y$, and lies in its maximal ideal whenever $f$ is not a unit of $O$, equals $b_x$;
--
--   5. if $c_x$ lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ then its $R_x$-residue is $0$;
--
--   6. if $c_y$ lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ then the order of its $R_x$-residue at $b_x$ is $1$.
--
--   At a node of the semistable model, with the crossing presentation $\hat O\cong \widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ and coordinates $c_x,c_y$, this produces the point of the reduced fibre cut out on the Igusa-side branch $W_x$: a rational place at which the node ring $O$ reduces with its nonunits going into the maximal ideal, uniquely determined by that, where the branch coordinate $c_x$ reduces to $0$ and the transverse coordinate $c_y$ reduces to a uniformiser. It is the Igusa-side counterpart of the statement centring the node ring on the supersingular branch, and it feeds the analysis of the Igusa end, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch).
